title: 'P8-D78/D79: Mac-first full loop, Windows later; LaunchServices open escape accepted'
summary: 'The founder sequenced Move 1 by platform and accepted the `open` residual. Next: spec v3.7 (probe evidence + D78/D79), PR-3 contracts and PR-5 daemon lifecycle in parallel, then PR-4 kernel log.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-harness'
decisions:
  - id: P8-D78
    decision: Build and test the full Move 1 loop on macOS first; Windows parity (helper, Hello/Passport KSP, WFP/AppContainer, pipes, the WebView2 wrapper, the Windows probes) is built when the founder is ready. Windows CI keeps running the platform-independent tests meanwhile. Move 1's pass is split by platform (macOS pass, then Windows parity pass). This is platform sequencing, not the alpha/beta/gamma checkpoints D57 declined.
    rationale: 'Founder: build and test the full loop on Mac, then build Windows when ready; no Windows machine is ready now.'
  - id: P8-D79
    decision: The macOS LaunchServices `open` escape (a sandboxed session can launch an unsandboxed app that reaches the endpoint port; no SBPL rule blocks it, per p10m) is ACCEPTED as a stated residual in §A.2. Presence (Touch ID on Reconnect/attach and on every gate) is the boundary.
    rationale: Founder accepted; no sandbox fix exists and the presence prompt already covers attach.
